# Grid / Aster Gateway — Frozen Chain

All changes (Aether, FIELD, Jarvis, UI, daemons, sidecars) **must not affect or touch** the Grid/Aster Gateway core inference and routing chain on **`:8501`**.

## Protected paths and behavior (do not modify)

- `/gateway`, `/chat`, `/v1/chat/completions`, `/api/v1/chat/completions`
- `/compile`, `/compile/first_proof`, `/cleanroom/*`
- `/challenge/*`, contract_gate, contract_lint, substrate pipeline
- `demo/aster` routing, token budget, concurrency slots, cleanroom gate
- `/store/events` write/read semantics and grid_store behavior
- Aster identity, system prompts, `unsafe_debug` / production routing policy

## Allowed without touching the chain

- New **read-only** routes on the same port (e.g. static trace index) that do not alter existing handlers
- Static files under `/app/*` (e.g. `aether.html`)
- Daemon emit payloads to `/store/events` (additive fields only)
- Separate ports/processes (`:8510`, `:8686`, `:8790`, etc.)

## When gateway code must change

1. **Do not edit** existing handler logic, middleware order, or routing for protected paths.
2. Prefer a **separate process or port** over changing `local_gateway.py` core.
3. If a read-only sidecar route is unavoidable: add isolated `GET` handlers only; no shared state changes; no model/substrate calls.
4. Never restart or reconfigure gateway as part of unrelated UI work unless the user explicitly approves.

**Enforcement (not agent memory):** `grid-infrastructure-immutable.mdc` · `config/grid_infrastructure_lock.json` · pre-commit · CI · `start_grid_gateway.sh verify-runtime`.

## Review checklist before any PR/commit

- [ ] No diff in protected handler bodies unless user explicitly requested gateway work
- [ ] No changes to Aster routing, contract gates, or compile/cleanroom
- [ ] Aether/daemon/UI changes use store emit or separate ports, not gateway inference paths
